[{:db/id "q-160450/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "8c36ecf4-ce53-5f85-858d-d4752fc8162b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160450/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "acf8bbfb-13a0-5fb4-8d9e-add9d122cf04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160450/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "550a56cd-0e38-5a5f-9c96-a336a635b67e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160450/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "289fd94c-d897-5b3c-9f9e-d9dc40c69681" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160450/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "de602220-a4c2-5ee6-8a1c-9b1364471cba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160450/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57833a01-d1ff-54d5-aa39-1e06e0d775aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160450/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-160450/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-160450/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-160450/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-160450/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-160450/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160450" :question/id #uuid "0680bfff-51f7-58c3-9dbe-9713d602a7d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-160450" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160450/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-154696"] :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1$, we have $f(x)={e}^{1-x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{1-x}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "0727cff0-8402-5226-9c30-edd3d293ff89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "af0c8623-4908-516b-9e9d-dfe7b43591b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "54cd70d8-b608-59d0-ad85-3beaf2aa4823" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b98f0199-cd39-5f46-9032-34fd4c4c28a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c762d5ab-1a2e-5a0b-a653-e611c868b48f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b6210cb-456a-574b-9d3f-31582abbcc58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160455/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-160455/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-160455/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-160455/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-160455/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-160455/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160455" :question/id #uuid "9d8aae59-53b9-5f80-8db0-b8e59b98bd0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160455" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{1-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=2{e}^{1-2x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }2{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160455/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f5bfded8-137f-569d-949e-481549c44b65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d2200014-ef31-5fc1-8821-00e2cd597fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "0e333a2e-4569-5f23-b8d5-8f3c8ed28a7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f5beb9b2-e403-541c-94a4-2b15238b4fdd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "11c2f7a8-e0f6-54e9-a62c-788e77ce82dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50c0df9a-5f39-59c9-9049-3b24e784608c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160447/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-160447/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-160447/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-160447/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-160447/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-160447/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160447" :question/id #uuid "576ea109-3051-59ce-a7ba-67047d37a95a" :question/math-academy-id "q-160447" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x/2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{x/2}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{e}^{x/2}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & =2({e}^{0}-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "f7c7d997-9138-54e9-8a49-acaae41087cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "3c778c8f-f3bb-5223-9289-d976e7a3b56b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e8b0162d-eb99-59e5-900f-fbc27d53cc2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ce3b999f-1664-5ae5-b147-57b350c7085f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d1b4a1c4-1508-597e-84bd-328f32a39659" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93534edc-2253-5472-b70f-366595869299" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160459/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-160459/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-160459/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-160459/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-160459/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-160459/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160459" :question/id #uuid "f8f4a5ce-40a5-520d-b284-4547a3fc3317" :question/math-academy-id "q-160459" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160459/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-86917"] :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{-3x}$ on the interval $0\\le x<\\infty ,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x={[-\\frac{k}{3}{e}^{-3x}]}_{0}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" :answer/id #uuid "6cd70fc6-5d73-58a7-bf28-b67e581cdd32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" :answer/id #uuid "1e5f1376-6a1e-5351-beea-d0f711e606a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469/selection/1cf7b6d0995d47b1afd89bc2301d308639c27c0926ad71ee7a6779958f73ef05" :answer/id #uuid "fe6d88e2-d1d8-553c-8342-0a80ac1615cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "810e6bf6-08cb-5b29-8a13-098f135356b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469/selection/a1a2c9254cf4541b376c718ee4aa2595e631729cb2d7ebbd92b4202d3d402d43" :answer/id #uuid "dc42ed7f-922f-5b9f-80a6-14a060310d87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39041751-656e-51f4-9429-ba9805f5e43e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160469/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" :answer-field/choices ["q-160469/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" "q-160469/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" "q-160469/selection/1cf7b6d0995d47b1afd89bc2301d308639c27c0926ad71ee7a6779958f73ef05" "q-160469/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" "q-160469/selection/a1a2c9254cf4541b376c718ee4aa2595e631729cb2d7ebbd92b4202d3d402d43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160469" :question/id #uuid "72cfc3d8-5a3c-5ad7-8fd8-90e82328cc82" :question/math-academy-id "q-160469" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{2-x},\\, & x\\ge -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{2-x}$ on the interval $x\\ge -1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=-k{e}^{2-x}\\,{|}_{-1}^{\\infty }=k{e}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk{e}^{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k={e}^{-3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160469/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec-e6753cc005a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160469"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160466/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "5509e390-3a9d-5bf2-a2d1-38c3bc97475f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160466/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "424e2858-e8ab-5e9e-accc-55d9dea2f0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-1