t{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{1-2x}$ on the interval $x\\ge 1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{2}{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{2e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{2e}=1\\,⟹\\,k=2e.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160466/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec-e6753cc005a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160466"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "d9d829d8-74d2-506e-b13e-e526b9f40473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "3aa97bad-0541-5aea-9ef2-a1670572c669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "fd2c70ef-e6d4-56c4-b25c-c98358523fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "6c39349d-4f94-5f50-9e08-5a9124bb68a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "8b3bc02e-7ff1-55aa-8c09-1ca2afa1ed0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3a0a15-9719-51ca-8483-7f960c2b8bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160463/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-160463/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-160463/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-160463/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-160463/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-160463/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160463" :question/id #uuid "2223100b-9916-59a8-976f-154591c025fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-160463" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}},\\, & x\\ge -2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}$ on the interval $x\\ge -2,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{6(x+3)^{6}}\\,{|}_{-2}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{6}=1\\,⟹\\,k=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160463/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec