:db/id "q-87238" :question/id #uuid "23fa3ed5-67fd-5567-92e1-2865c6e59cbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-87238" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-5x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{-5x}$ on the interval $0\\le x<\\infty ,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x={[-\\frac{k}{5}{e}^{-5x}]}_{0}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{5}=1\\,⟹\\,k=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87238/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec-e6753cc005a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87238"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219/selection/c5a0007895a0b33276781a155ddb1d83be3c93a909759a21526781541fd41e06" :answer/id #uuid "9d594cc2-82ab-5d72-aba5-2c2f27bdbf9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219/selection/ad7063a3c34601eaafe6672dc55056fa1174aa89410d87b6bbab21cdb4f60077" :answer/id #uuid "6d3f9c4b-863b-544a-9960-4043155fc2ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" :answer/id #uuid "3f5b8585-faf2-5a24-bf82-bfa372632f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219/selection/811ec39bff7c24334c7effa9f110af6c704bbebb27ff9d16b166d96bfc229e79" :answer/id #uuid "9736207c-e353-5335-9326-acdc04967c29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219/selection/ccf161765e92a59547a3a6375eb736f8e16993466ceab93d5323fb8e432cca9e" :answer/id #uuid "e7750519-78a4-59eb-8a98-4e5189db8550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65b0293b-32c4-5c89-8f3c-e0b208f894f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87219/selection/ad7063a3c34601eaafe6672dc55056fa1174aa89410d87b6bbab21cdb4f60077" :answer-field/choices ["q-87219/selection/c5a0007895a0b33276781a155ddb1d83be3c93a909759a21526781541fd41e06" "q-87219/selection/ad7063a3c34601eaafe6672dc55056fa1174aa89410d87b6bbab21cdb4f60077" "q-87219/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" "q-87219/selection/811ec39bff7c24334c7effa9f110af6c704bbebb27ff9d16b166d96bfc229e79" "q-87219/selection/ccf161765e92a59547a3a6375eb736f8e16993466ceab93d5323fb8e432cca9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87219" :question/id #uuid "c18e7418-d781-59f4-9d8f-d01f265d2cb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-87219" :question/problem "Compute $P(X>6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(6<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }3{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-3x}]}_{6}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87219/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016/selection/de2f9e8d93e24093f903d192e87652a275278440944fbfbf925ef2d61e21dc26" :answer/id #uuid "4f6d9e2f-a6ca-56f8-b684-0969fd6e8bd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" :answer/id #uuid "de704ba8-b32b-5116-8c83-4ff57be8cb22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016/selection/77c4b3dafbc3d48ea91ae6461ab3b59b2507d0ac081191aa6e18cbc5b60fc530" :answer/id #uuid "e896bd42-ce89-5980-abed-680138a7c92f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016/selection/fcc279f4d796f8ff9280439b2f7a5e3d2d8beb45233f02d00bcd92c2b267f6f8" :answer/id #uuid "6ff5d366-f3f0-58f2-ab45-399c4d3a5a82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" :answer/id #uuid "1487d4df-e3bd-5585-b21c-dfe4c3398ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c802a245-15a1-5149-9a06-be5c2b0a3b42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126016/selection/de2f9e8d93e24093f903d192e87652a275278440944fbfbf925ef2d61e21dc26" :answer-field/choices ["q-126016/selection/de2f9e8d93e24093f903d192e87652a275278440944fbfbf925ef2d61e21dc26" "q-126016/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" "q-126016/selection/77c4b3dafbc3d48ea91ae6461ab3b59b2507d0ac081191aa6e18cbc5b60fc530" "q-126016/selection/fcc279f4d796f8ff9280439b2f7a5e3d2d8beb45233f02d00bcd92c2b267f6f8" "q-126016/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126016" :question/id #uuid "87ab5e1a-40f2-585e-8f36-c410606655e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126016" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =P(3\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}]}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126016/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126016"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-86914"] :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =P(5\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-8x}]}_{5}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032/selection/d5f60636dd9bb4c398339fd4cfb9d759962c28276d898062e3a89bd03c2f9932" :answer/id #uuid "51a7f16e-7442-5559-8f3f-524f3bd117ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032/selection/a6c24763be7bc10534ff181db6f9bbc4ce5918a064f5ae69027c6cc73fedb0f0" :answer/id #uuid "bbf31511-480a-57f7-9483-3c605b3c70ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032/selection/ec10a4ad99b8bdb716bfab5c12874cbe6f60f78c832a4d5ede20b439810561b8" :answer/id #uuid "ff65de56-572e-5a0d-9118-63fe1e6e6cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" :answer/id #uuid "d6061aec-ac09-5016-a963-b7282c213250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c" :answer/id #uuid "791c624b-10bd-5dbd-bc9e-42b30f2fff9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23211f8b-aa86-54be-8e78-65e6a541a77c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126032/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-126032/selection/d5f60636dd9bb4c398339fd4cfb9d759962c28276d898062e3a89bd03c2f9932" "q-126032/selection/a6c24763be7bc10534ff181db6f9bbc4ce5918a064f5ae69027c6cc73fedb0f0" "q-126032/selection/ec10a4ad99b8bdb716bfab5c12874cbe6f60f78c832a4d5ede20b439810561b8" "q-126032/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" "q-126032/selection/a60c74b10dbfeb18f6554b820139a05af96cf3f33173758365535188f3be0c1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126032" :question/id #uuid "2191f3b5-f79c-5fb9-91eb-b95fdad50ac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126032" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(2\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{2-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{2-2x}]}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126032/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018/selection/398debd424cf862b5e5b460c0b8b7be9a2496463c25f61a9599ca303792a0c28" :answer/id #uuid "4e039e7a-2583-5028-8302-700c2b53fa1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-0.1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" :answer/id #uuid "0c590bfc-8376-5255-a29e-4f09fe6485dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018/selection/3b7873f8a9598ff5d704fc37848f14cdd0f5b07e0c7f84ab8f4dd30d5282d068" :answer/id #uuid "d1282e1c-7dea-5f41-9355-19945b7c2a87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-0.1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018/selection/77a4d1614a31984fd7a1830286b83cb9f7c97cb3854a84de04924da94780e2f9" :answer/id #uuid "04518b46-838e-5873-bb77-7410af4ef989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-0.3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018/selection/b3469628fb57106dfde8ee61b187a7df37d8d6eb97fa633c700260f26b57fd74" :answer/id #uuid "747860c1-d1fe-50f4-a29e-7839415e08a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{0.1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec131ce1-6f7a-5d0d-bdef-856d2c27772b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126018/selection/398debd424cf862b5e5b460c0b8b7be9a2496463c25f61a9599ca303792a0c28" :answer-field/choices ["q-126018/selection/398debd424cf862b5e5b460c0b8b7be9a2496463c25f61a9599ca303792a0c28" "q-126018/selection/538c8670cb439d1a98a40b4c40205e43f4702337d59966894e4057eb0e28d3b2" "q-126018/selection/3b7873f8a9598ff5d704fc37848f14cdd0f5b07e0c7f84ab8f4dd30d5282d068" "q-126018/selection/77a4d1614a31984fd7a1830286b83cb9f7c97cb3854a84de04924da94780e2f9" "q-126018/selection/b3469628fb57106dfde8ee61b187a7df37d8d6eb97fa633c700260f26b57fd74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126018" :question/id #uuid "fb744e8a-ff2d-5960-83aa-70c9996a145a" :question/math-academy-id "q-126018" :question/problem "Compute $P(X>1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0.1{e}^{-0.1x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & =P(1<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }0.1{e}^{-0.1x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-0.1x}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-0.1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126018/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126018"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12329"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/assets/d6ad9cbcf369609541984bb88a414653161a9ed723ec2637d6e73cc81b62a238.png)\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\geq 3$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^{\\infty} f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x = 1$\n\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x \\geq 3,$ we have $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{(x-2)^2} \\geq 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }(x-2)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10851"] :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/assets/0ba485cc9b536bd1a7cd18f37c61d269515b2bcb621cabfa55d6a567d53144c6.png)" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3}$ on the interval $x \\geq 0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3} \\, \\textrm dx = 1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(4x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{[\\frac{k}{8(4x+1)^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{8} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad k = 8.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-10840"] :question/problem "Compute $P\\left( X > 8 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062347/assets/cc8c2867f9ef99a8c476feeb319e03a3a479dd23f04e546bf1e5240daa4ea0ac.png)" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a <    X <    b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }5{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-5x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
